<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Arthur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1784–1854</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Arthur was a British army officer and colonial governor. He served as superintendent of British Honduras from 1814 to 1822, where he clashed with the settlers over their treatment of enslaved people. As lieutenant governor of Van Diemen's Land from 1824 to 1836 he built a strict convict system and directed the Black War against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-tasmanians">Aboriginal Tasmanians</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-arthur.jpg" alt="George Arthur" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Major-General_Sir_George_Arthur_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
